<title>BELGIUM: Commission clears Allianz control of Hermes.</title>
<headline>Commission clears Allianz control of Hermes.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it had cleared an agreement under which German insurer Allianz acquires control of Hermes, another German insurance company previously owned by Munich Re.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement it had cleared the deal because it would result in &quot;no or only insignificant additions of market shares&quot;.</p>
<p>This was particularly the case in Germany, where Hermes, a leading European credit insurance firm, does most of its business, it said.</p>
<p>Under a shareholding swap between Allianz AG Holding and Munich Re AG, the parent of Hermes Kredit Versicherungs AG, Allianz increases its participation in Hermes to a majority stake.</p>
</text>
